# LeakSanitizer suppressions of the sanitizer job (Script/linux_jobs.sh sanitizers and the "sanitizers"
# job of .github/workflows/analysis.yml; docs/refactor/PLAN.md, 1.5b-5).
#
# Only leaks whose cause is inside third-party code are listed, each with its reason. A leak in our own
# code is fixed, not suppressed; so is an SDL or OpenAL object that we created and never destroyed. A new
# third-party report goes here with the stack it stands for.
#
# Format: leak:<name of a function that is in the leak's stack>. A suppression hides every leak (and
# everything it points to) whose stack passes through that function, so the entry names the SDL function
# that calls into the library: the frames inside Mesa and ALSA stay "<unknown module>" in a report,
# because SDL loads them with dlopen and unloads them again before the leak check.
#
# Each entry was shown to be needed (the row returns without it) and to be a library's doing: a plain SDL
# program (window and renderer, a texture copy and present, an audio device opened and closed, then
# destroyed, SDL_Quit) leaks the same blocks with the same stacks. The run prints which entries it used
# ("Suppressions used:" at the end of the log of a process).

# SDL's offscreen video driver (what SDL picks without a display, as on CI) initialises EGL for the
# OpenGL renderer; Mesa's libEGL allocates the EGL display and does not free it.
#   Direct leak of 2680 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:
#     #0 calloc  #1..#3 <unknown module> (libEGL)
#     #4 SDL_EGL_InitializeOffscreen  #5 OFFSCREEN_GLES_LoadLibrary  #6 SDL_GL_LoadLibrary
#     #7 SDL_RecreateWindow  #8 GL_CreateRenderer  #9 SDL_CreateRenderer
#     #10 SDLRendererGraphicsDriver::SetDisplayMode  Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp:146
leak:SDL_EGL_InitializeOffscreen

# The first draw call through that OpenGL renderer makes Mesa's software rasteriser allocate two blocks of
# 56 bytes that it does not free; they point to each other, so LSan reports them as indirect leaks only.
#   Indirect leak of 56 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:    (twice)
#     #0 calloc  #1..#16 <unknown module> (Mesa)
#     #17 GL_RunCommandQueue  #18 FlushRenderCommands  #19 FlushRenderCommandsIfNotBatching
#     #20 SDL_RenderCopyF  ...  SDLRendererGraphicsDriver::Present  Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp:762
leak:GL_RunCommandQueue

# Opening an audio device with SDL's ALSA driver: libasound allocates its configuration (2049 blocks,
# 66666 bytes in one run, 16 bytes of them direct) and does not free it when the device is closed. The
# engine opens the device and closes it at once (try_init_audio_driver, SDL_CloseAudioDevice) and calls
# SDL_QuitSubSystem(SDL_INIT_AUDIO).
#   Direct leak of 16 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:
#     #0 calloc  #1..#3 <unknown module> (libasound)
#     #4 ALSA_OpenDevice  #5 open_audio_device  #6 try_init_audio_driver
#     Engine/platform/base/sys_main.cpp:194
leak:ALSA_OpenDevice
